<title>UK: Ex-dividends to take 2.857 points off FTSE, June 9.</title>
<headline>Ex-dividends to take 2.857 points off FTSE, June 9.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following FTSE-100 stocks will go ex-dividend on Monday and analysts estimate this will take 2.857 points off the index at the start of trading on June 9.</p>
<p>							DIVIDEND     INDEX</p>
<p>							(PENCE)	EFFECT</p>
<p>	   COMPANY				 Net   Gross    Gross</p>
<p> * Burmah Castrol		   (a)   31.000    0.372</p>
<p> * National Grid Group	     6.68   8.350    0.827</p>
<p> * United Utilities		  25.20  31.500    0.977</p>
<p> * Vodafone Group plc	  VOD .L     2.45   3.062    0.545</p>
<p> * Wolseley PLC			3.30   4.125    0.136</p>
<p>(a) For Burmah Castrol there is a Foreign Income Dividend (FID) of 31p only.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
